# UI Styling with Tailwind CSS

## Structure vs theme
- **Structure is fixed; theme is swappable:** token architecture and accessibility rules are inherited; token values are re-skinned per product.
- **Mobile-first responsive:** design from smallest breakpoint up using Tailwind utility classes.

## Semantic Tokens (required)
- Use semantic CSS variables from [`src/app/globals.css`](../../src/app/globals.css) (`bg-background`, `text-foreground`, etc.) — see [AGENTS.md § Hard constraints](../../AGENTS.md#hard-constraints)
- Token architecture and re-skin workflow: [`DESIGN.md`](../../DESIGN.md)
- Never hardcode theme colors (raw hex or numeric Tailwind color scales for themeable color)

## Theming
- Dark mode via `next-themes` in [`src/providers/ThemeProvider.tsx`](../../src/providers/ThemeProvider.tsx)
- shadcn/ui uses **CSS variables** for theming (configured in `components.json`)
- Colors use semantic tokens (`bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `border-border`) — variables switch automatically in light/dark mode
- Manual dark-mode classes rarely needed with shadcn components

## Utilities & Layout
- Use `cn()` from [`@/utils/tailwind`](../../src/utils/tailwind.ts) for conditional class merging
- Follow Tailwind's spacing scale consistently (4, 8, 12, 16, etc.)
- Component organization: reusable in `src/components/`, shadcn primitives in `src/components/ui/`, page-specific in `src/app/[page]/_components/`

## Image Optimization
- Use Next.js `Image` component for all images
- Include size data (width/height) to prevent layout shift
- Implement lazy loading for below-the-fold images; use `priority` for above-the-fold

## Best Practices
- ✅ Use CSS variables for theming (already configured)
- ✅ Follow mobile-first responsive approach
- ✅ Use semantic spacing scale
- ✅ Optimize images with Next.js Image component
- ❌ Don't fight the CSS variables system for theming
- ❌ Don't hardcode colors; use theme variables
- ❌ Don't skip image dimensions (causes layout shift)
